    "body": "Ah, sorry, I didn't check the test carefully enough to understand what it did. OK so `link rel=stylesheet` and `script` are tested. Great! Thanks for filing the wpt issue also.\n\nSo if this only works for stylesheet `link`s, I think it should be made non-conforming to specify the attribute if the `rel` attribute does not contain the `stylesheet` keyword.\n\nSimilarly for `script`, if it only applies to classic scripts, it should be non-conforming to specify it for module scripts. (The patch already makes it non-conforming for data blocks, which is good.)\n",
